 earn profit and pay twenty six  percent or earn profit and pay twenty  two percent what do I choose I choose  twenty two percent the lower effective  tax rate is an incentive for me not to  invest in the business remember if I  invest in the business I lower the  adjusted income that saves me more if  the tax rate is higher I am more  incentivized to reinvest in my business  if there is a higher effective tax rate  it's just a fundamental backwards  element of the entire right wing view  around taxation this year I paid  thirteen percent less on the profit that  the business earned it's an incentive  not to reinvest there's no economically  defensible reason for my tax rate to  have dropped thirteen percent despite  the fact that the david pakman show grew  and this applies to so many of the  businesses that we are told if we just  cut their taxes it's gonna be great for  the economy it's going to be good for  everybody it's going to lead to hiring  it's gonna pump money into the economy  it's not I wasn't planning on that tax  return I am NOT spending on the  assumption that I am getting that tax  refund not return and it's simply not  better for the economy now you might say  David well then just send in more money  to the federal government that's not tax  policy me choosing to pay twenty six  percent instead of twenty two percent  that's not policy that's not money that  the government has budgeted for it's not  money that would be used in any  productive way when it's not actually  expected to be tax revenues on the basis  of a broader tax plan me sending in more  money is is just one of those ridiculous  right-wing sort of libertarian ish  cartoonish ideas doesn't make sense but  case in point why these tax cuts for  corporations are not good for the  economy
 

